      "writtenOn": "2020-09-09T06:01:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This code means you can\u0027t distinguish between a network that won\u0027t perform validation (e.g. a network that doesn\u0027t offer INTERNET connectivity) from a network that did but the validation was skipped this time. Is this okay with your intended use ? For the API in general I\u0027m not sure this is a great implication.\n\nNote that importantly this will mean the latest connectivity report stored in the NAI will now have this bit. Therefore :\n• Some network comes up and validates\n• GMSCore or somebody else calls reportNetworkConnectivity(true)\n• This code skips validation, because it\u0027s already what we knew\n• An administrator apps registers for a connectivity report\n• The administrator apps gets told that validation was skipped\n\nIs this what you intend ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4386,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 4386,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "ca543bf11dfb15655ceaceb90e7a06cd31d3f51c",
